lementary":0,"rejected":0,"closed":16,"total":16},{"year":2023,"recognized":0,"complementary":0,"rejected":0,"closed":42,"total":42},{"year":2024,"recognized":0,"complementary":0,"rejected":0,"closed":39,"total":39},{"year":2025,"recognized":0,"complementary":0,"rejected":0,"closed":78,"total":78}]},"per_1000":{"year":2025,"value":0.48,"numerator":4893,"denominator":10246996,"sources":["unhcr-pop-2026","wb-pop-2026"],"note":"Refugees per 1,000 people living in Azerbaijan."}},"headlines":{"over_time":{"text":"Ukrainian refugees in Azerbaijan rose from {n0} (2014) to a peak of {n1} (2024)","nums":[0,4906],"years":[2014,2024]},"where_people_are":{"text":"Azerbaijan hosts {p0} of all Ukrainian refugees (2025), up from {p1} in 2022","pcts":[0.1,0.1],"years":[2025,2022]}},"steps":{"brief":true,"key_numbers":true,"over_time":true,"where_people_are":true,"inside_outside":true,"compare":false,"context":true,"other_angles":true,"limitations":true,"sources":true},"brief_sources":[],"footnotes":{"fn_04e84f68":"Start-year figures come from the 2009 census, reporting 3585 stateless persons. In 2023, UNHCR conducted an extensive identification exercise of stateless persons in Azerbaijan using both government and UNHCR registers. The exercise was able to account for 513 stateless person. The government of Azerbaijan confirmed that between 2008 and 2023, 2306 stateless persons aquired citizenship of Azerbaijan.","fn_132a361b":"IDP figure in Ukraine includes 800,000 people who are in an IDP-like situation.","fn_15e33dc9":"The IDP figure has been aligned to the inter-agency methodology as defined in the 2020 Humanitarian Needs Overview. Figure of others of concern relates to persons who have specific protection needs and live in non-government-controlled areas or within 20 km of the contact line in government-controlled areas.","fn_1cbda1a3":"Figure from the 2009 census.","fn_2462913e":"Figure from 2009 census. 1,640 persons were registered by the Ministry of Interior as stateless at the end of 2012.","fn_33d9bf20":"Figure from the 2009 census.","fn_3e8e7fae":"The IDP figure has been aligned to the inter-agency methodology as defined in the 2020 Humanitarian Needs Overview. Figure of others of concern relates to persons who have specific protection needs and live in non-government-controlled areas or within 20 km of the contact line in government-controlled areas.","fn_4f6fe86c":"Temporary protection granted to Ukrainians does not necessarily mean new displacement since it could include reapplications or reactivations from the refugees who were already granted refugee status following temporary visits to Ukraine as well as duplicated registrations across countries. Furthermore, Ukrainians that have been granted temporary protection may also have lodged individual asylum applications. See Ukraine Refugee Situation: Population movements, Factsheet #2, UNHCR (https://data.unhcr.org/en/documents/details/114591).","fn_588219b5":"All figures are as of mid-2025.","fn_5c2cef73":"Figure from 2009 census. 1,640 persons were registered by the Ministry of Interior as stateless at the end of 2012.","fn_5d5a5199":"UNHCR continues to report on the 2,534 refugees and 36,241 stateless people until their status and whereabouts can be ascertained. For asylum-seekers, end of year figures account also for those who confirmed their spontaneous departure to UNHCR from February 2022. The others of concern figure at end-2022 corresponds to the number of conflict-affected, non-displaced people assisted by UNHCR during the year.","fn_6e0523b1":"IDP figure in Ukraine includes 800,000 people who are in an IDP-like situation.","fn_7dcf65e3":"The IDP figure has been aligned to the inter-agency methodology as defined in the 2020 Humanitarian Needs Overview. Figure of others of concern relates to persons who have specific protection needs and live in non-government-controlled areas or within 20 km of the contact line in government-controlled areas.","fn_85797c16":"Temporary protection granted to Ukrainians does not necessarily mean new displacement since it could include reapplications or reactivations from the refugees who were already granted refugee status following temporary visits to Ukraine as well as duplicated registrations across countries. Furthermore, Ukrainians that have been granted temporary protection may also have lodged individual asylum applications. See Ukraine Refugee Situation: Population movements, Factsheet #2, UNHCR (https://data.unhcr.org/en/documents/details/114591).","fn_911d1c29":"All figures are as of mid-2025.","fn_9dafdd55":"Figure from the 2009 census.","fn_a6e0c6ad":"Figure from the 2009 census.","fn_b51ae7ac":"Figure from the 2009 census.","fn_b531e02e":"IDP figure in Ukraine includes 800,000 people who are in an IDP-like situation.","fn_bbd9f1f0":"Since February 2022, a number of Ukrainians have reached countries beyond Europe, where they are staying under various legal statuses. See UNHCR’s Ukraine Situation Operational Data Portal for up-to date statistics of refugees from Ukraine recorded in Europe and beyond.","fn_bf8a15ce":"All figures are as of mid-2025.  Since 2023, the number of stateless persons in Azerbaijan is based on government (State Migration Service and the Ministry of Internal Affairs) and UNHCR registers.","fn_d43080db":"Figure from 2009 census. 1,640 persons were registered by the Ministry of Interior as stateless at the end of 2012.","fn_d6187d44":"UNHCR continues to report on the 2,534 refugees and 36,241 stateless people until their status and whereabouts can be ascertained. For asylum-seekers, end of year figures account also for those who confirmed their spontaneous departure to UNHCR from February 2022. The others of concern figure at end-2022 corresponds to the number of conflict-affected, non-displaced people assisted by UNHCR during the year.","fn_dc879acb":"In 2023, UNHCR conducted an extensive identification exercise of stateless persons in Azerbaijan using both government and UNHCR registers. The exercise was able to account for 513 stateless person, which was used as the start year figure. During 2024, 306 individuals at risk of statelessness were able to acquire citizenship. Additional persons of undetermined nationality were identified during the year, resulting in a total of 271 stateless persons in the country at end-year based on information from the State Migration Service, the Ministry of Internal Affairs and UNHCR.","fn_ddfa157e":"IDP figure in Ukraine includes 700,000 people who are in an IDP-like situation.","fn_ea267799":"IDP figure in Ukraine includes 800,000 people who are in an IDP-like situation.","fn_f0980c35":"The IDP figure has been aligned to the inter-agency methodology as defined in the 2022 Humanitarian Needs Overview, including an area-based improvement of the estimation of people displaced in government-controlled areas. The others of concern figure relates to persons who have specific protection needs and live in non-government-controlled areas."},"raw_files":{"conflict.csv":{"label":"IDMC GIDD, conflict and violence (HDX csv)","header":["iso3","country_name","year","new_displacement","new_displacement_rounded","total_displacement","total_displacement_rounded"]},"demographics/2025.zip":{"label":"UNHCR API download (demographics/2025.zip)","header":["Year","Country of origin","Country of origin (ISO)","Country of asylum","Country of asylum (ISO)","Population Type","Female 0 - 4","Female 5 - 11","Female 12 - 17","Female 18 - 59","Female 60","Female other","Female total","Male 0 - 4","Male 5 - 11","Male 12 - 17","Male 18 - 59","Male 60","Male other","Male total","Total"]},"persons_of_concern.csv":{"label":"UNHCR Refugee Data Finder download (persons_of_concern.csv)","header":["Year","Country of Asylum","Country of Origin","Country of Asylum ISO","Country of Origin ISO","Refugees","Asylum-seekers","IDPs","Other people in need of international protection","Stateless persons","Host community","Others of concern"]},